      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that suggestions like finding \"hobbies\" feel dismissive when your entire sense of purpose was tied to someone else. This feeling of erasure suggests a deeper crisis of identity, not just sadness. Instead of searching for a replacement passion, focus on small acts of rediscovery that require no external validation—like noticing the color of the sky or the sound of the rain. Allow yourself the space to simply *be* without the pressure of needing to be \"someone\" right now.",
